{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00672",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.3,
      "end_seconds": 12.43,
      "duration_seconds": 11.13,
      "text": "Mr Whitlock, thank you for coming. The booking says you want to go over how cardiac rehab is going. Fair?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.35,
      "end_seconds": 24.11,
      "duration_seconds": 8.76,
      "text": "Yes. I brought my diary, I've written down everything since the eight-week mark. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.76,
      "end_seconds": 32.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.59,
      "text": "Excellent. Start with breathlessness, you said that was your main thing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.22,
      "end_seconds": 47.23,
      "duration_seconds": 14.01,
      "text": "Breathlessness on the stairs is much better. In January I had to stop halfway, now I can do the lot at home without stopping."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.75,
      "end_seconds": 55.99,
      "duration_seconds": 6.24,
      "text": "Good. And how are your energy levels through the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.13,
      "end_seconds": 65.77,
      "duration_seconds": 8.64,
      "text": "Tired in the afternoons, about three days a week. I note it in the diary."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.69,
      "end_seconds": 71.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Any swelling around the ankles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.46,
      "end_seconds": 80.15,
      "duration_seconds": 7.69,
      "text": "A little at night, on the left. It's gone by the morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.42,
      "end_seconds": 85.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "Any odd fluttering in the chest?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 87.33,
      "end_seconds": 94.19,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Twice. Last Tuesday and the week before, a few seconds each."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.65,
      "end_seconds": 101.74,
      "duration_seconds": 6.09,
      "text": "Have you had any chest pain since the programme began?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.21,
      "end_seconds": 105.5,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "No, none whatsoever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.08,
      "end_seconds": 111.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "Any fainting or blackouts?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.52,
      "end_seconds": 116.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 118.29,
      "end_seconds": 121.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Right. Let's go through your tablets."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 123.74,
      "end_seconds": 137.04,
      "duration_seconds": 13.3,
      "text": "Bisoprolol, 2.5 mg, once a day. Ramipril, I think it's maybe 5 mg, I'd have to look at the packet. And atorvastatin, 40 mg, at night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.48,
      "end_seconds": 146.74,
      "duration_seconds": 7.26,
      "text": "We'll check the ramipril dose against your record. Any allergies to medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.45,
      "end_seconds": 151.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "No, I have no allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.71,
      "end_seconds": 157.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.23,
      "text": "Good. Tell me your heart history again, for my notes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 160.85,
      "end_seconds": 169.25,
      "duration_seconds": 8.4,
      "text": "I had a heart attack, last summer. I have high blood pressure, high cholesterol, and sleep apnoea."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.45,
      "end_seconds": 172.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "And any procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 173.62,
      "end_seconds": 181.42,
      "duration_seconds": 7.8,
      "text": "They put in a stent, eight months ago. And my gallbladder was taken out in 2012."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.14,
      "end_seconds": 185.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "Any heart disease in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.0,
      "end_seconds": 191.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "My father had a heart attack at fifty-five."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.36,
      "end_seconds": 197.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.99,
      "text": "You used to smoke, didn't you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.2,
      "end_seconds": 206.5,
      "duration_seconds": 6.3,
      "text": "I stopped smoking the day after the heart attack. Not one since."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.24,
      "end_seconds": 210.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.07,
      "text": "Alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 211.92,
      "end_seconds": 219.92,
      "duration_seconds": 8.0,
      "text": "I drink one pint of beer on a Friday. Under the limit, I made sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.65,
      "end_seconds": 224.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "And how's the exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 225.49,
      "end_seconds": 233.53,
      "duration_seconds": 8.04,
      "text": "I walk forty minutes every morning, and the rehab classes twice a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 250.52,
      "end_seconds": 264.08,
      "duration_seconds": 13.56,
      "text": "Let me do your numbers. Pulse is 58, which is expected on bisoprolol, blood pressure 126 over 74, temperature 36.4, oxygen 98 percent, breathing 14, and weight 84 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 266.16,
      "end_seconds": 270.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "Down two kilos from March. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.99,
      "end_seconds": 286.45,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "Well done. Let me listen to your chest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.65,
      "end_seconds": 291.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Take your time. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.0,
      "end_seconds": 300.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.76,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal, regular rhythm, and the lungs are clear on both sides."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.3,
      "end_seconds": 305.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Good to hear. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.55,
      "end_seconds": 313.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Your ankles, there's mild swelling at the left ankle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 315.96,
      "end_seconds": 318.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "That's what I noted. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.45,
      "end_seconds": 325.98,
      "duration_seconds": 5.53,
      "text": "And any trouble with your breathing at rest?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 327.23,
      "end_seconds": 330.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "No, nothing. Breathing's fine at rest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.67,
      "end_seconds": 342.13,
      "duration_seconds": 10.46,
      "text": "You're making good progress after the heart attack. The flutters are probably benign extra beats, but I'd like to look properly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 342.99,
      "end_seconds": 346.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "How do you do that? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.12,
      "end_seconds": 358.26,
      "duration_seconds": 11.14,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an ECG today, a 24-hour heart monitor, and an echocardiogram to check how strong the heart muscle is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.24,
      "end_seconds": 363.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "When will the monitor be? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.73,
      "end_seconds": 370.4,
      "duration_seconds": 5.67,
      "text": "The nurses will fit it before you go. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 371.18,
      "end_seconds": 374.2,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Good. And rehab continues? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.24,
      "end_seconds": 380.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.99,
      "text": "Absolutely, keep walking and keep attending the classes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 381.41,
      "end_seconds": 383.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "I will. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 385.12,
      "end_seconds": 397.03,
      "duration_seconds": 11.91,
      "text": "I'll see you again if the flutters get more frequent or the swelling doesn't settle in four weeks. Otherwise carry on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 398.94,
      "end_seconds": 401.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "Understood. Thank you. ~"
    }
  ]
}
